      "message": "fix(sim): weight the B letter by |cos A| in the mid-pose swing bound\n\nThe mid-pose walk bounds the axis turn inside an interval by the\nletters' sweep, each letter at one radian for each radian. B turns the\naxis only |cos A| for each radian. axis_to_angles writes a radial pose\nunder the A line as B180 and over it as B0, so at A = -90 one pose\nflips B by 180. The old bound read that flip as a 90 degree swing. The\nposed fixture sweep then grew the spindle housing capsule by hundreds\nof mm into the machine table, and the post refused a legal Rotary Flow\non a turning A with \"spindle housing at move N strikes a fixture\".\n\nThe bound now counts B at the largest |cos A| the move holds. It is\nstill a proven upper bound, so every law that reads the swing keeps\nenclosing the true sweep.\n\nFixes #4262\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
